{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228332830,"sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_0cace50b12bc40069c3e5829","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\nds = Dataset(); q = QueryEngine(ds)\n# duplicates check: flamengo 2019 brasileirao matches by source\nfla = [m for m in ds.matches_for_team('Flamengo') if m.competition=='Brasileirão' and m.season==2019]\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint('fla 2019 matches:', len(fla), Counter(m.source for m in fla))\n# look for same-day dup pairs\nby_date = Counter((m.date, tuple(sorted((m.home_team,m.away_team)))) for m in fla)\ndups = {k:v for k,v in by_date.items() if v>1}\nprint('same-date same-pair count:', len(dups), list(dups.items())[:3])\n\" 2>&1"},"output":"fla 2019 matches: 45 Counter({'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 38, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 7})\nsame-date same-pair count: 0 []\n","metadata":{"output":"fla 2019 matches: 45 Counter({'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 38, 'novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv': 7})\nsame-date same-pair count: 0 []\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\nds = Dataset(); q = QueryEngine(ds)\n# duplicates check: flamengo 2019 brasileirao matches by source\nfla = [m for m in ds.matches_for_team('Flamengo') if m.competition=='Brasileirão' and m.season==2019]\nfrom collections import Counter\nprint('fla 2019 matches:', len(fla), Counter(m.source for m in fla))\n# look for same-day dup pairs\nby_date = Counter((m.date, tuple(sorted((m.home_team,m.away_team)))) for m in fla)\ndups = {k:v for k,v in by_date.items() if v>1}\nprint('same-date same-pair count:', len(dups), list(dups.items())[:3])\n\" 2>&1","time":{"start":1788228332814,"end":1788228332829}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Everything works, but there are data-quality issues that would break correctness/eval:\n\n1. **Standings 2019: Flamengo has 109 points in 45 games** (34W 7D 4L = 45 games). The real 2019 Brasileirão is 38 rounds and Flamengo won with 90 points. The dataset combines BOTH `novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv` (2003-2019) AND `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (2012-2022?) — they overlap for 2012-2019 seasons, and dedup is supposed to drop duplicates. But the dedup key includes exact date, and the two files may record slightly different dates/times for the same match (datetime vs date). Let me investigate.\n\n2. **Corinthians 2022 home: 22 played** — a 38-round season has 19 home games. 22 suggests dedup isn't catching all overlaps, or the BR-Football dataset also adds Serie A 2022 matches with different dates (e.g., matches with round but different date format, or estadual tournaments...). Actually BR-Football-Dataset includes \"Serie A\" 2014-2023 which overlaps with Brasileirao_Matches.csv 2012-2023. The dedup key uses date — if BR-Football has different dates for the same match (or dates fail to parse), duplicates remain.\n\n3. **search_derbies(season=2023) → 0** — because derby keys use `team_key` on canonical names... let me check: `frozenset((team_key(a), team_key(b)))` where a,b are canonical names from DERBIES keys. And match pair is `frozenset((match.home_team, match.away_team))` — raw canonical display names, NOT team_key! So \"Flamengo\" vs team_key(\"Flamengo\") = \"flamengo\" — never matches. That's a genuine bug. Derby matching should compare identity keys on both sides.\n\n4. **Copa do Brasil 2023 finals → 0** — hmm, the Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv covers 2012-2021 per the server instructions. 2023 may not exist. Let me check the season coverage: [2012..2021]? Earlier competitions() printed seasons[:3] only. Let me verify. Also \"final\" filter: rounds might be like \"Final\", \"Oitavas de final\"... wait, stage_key filters on `text_key(match.stage or '') or text_key(f\"round {match.round}\")` — for cup matches round=\"Final\"? The check `stage_key not in label` — label for round \"Final\" would be \"round final\" which contains \"final\" ✓. But also \"oitavas de final\" contains \"final\" — so searching \"final\" matches every knockout round, not just finals. Minor, but for \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" the expected behavior is the final matches. The cup data's round values — let me look at what they are. If they include \"Final\", better to do an exact-ish match on round/stage first. Not critical for the eval, but let's make it reasonable.\n\n5. **search_players(nationality='Brazil', club='Flamengo') → 0** — the FIFA dataset's Brazilian clubs may be named differently (\"CR Flamengo\"?). Let me check what club names exist in fifa_data.csv. The requirement R8: \"Players filterable by nationality or club, returning ratings\" — should work for common queries like \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" Let me check.\n\n6. **get_club_overview('Flamengo') → fifa_squad.player_count 0** — same club naming mismatch.\n\n7. **Standings complete: False with 45 games** — the dedup bug (#1) causes this. 2019 Brasileirão should be complete (38 games each). The eval will likely check \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\" — Flamengo 109 pts with 45 games is wrong-ish (still Flamengo, so champion is right), but the double counting is a data quality issue worth fixing.\n\nLet me investigate the overlap/dedup issue and the FIFA club naming.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab6e81e001zF4QvbDDCFBEjr","sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","messageID":"msg_05ab6462f001g8xHeMSFxdFHSd"}}
