{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228515376,"sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_2aee9163e16847afa8829bb7","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('rounds:', Counter(r['round'] for r in rows))\nprint('seasons:', sorted({r['season'] for r in rows}))\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('stages:', Counter(r['stage'] for r in rows).most_common(20))\n\""},"output":"rounds: Counter({'2': 376, '1': 334, '3': 258, '4': 140, '5': 123, '6': 62, '7': 30, '8': 14})\nseasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\nstages: [('group stage', 960), ('round of 16', 160), ('quarterfinals', 80), ('semifinals', 40), ('final', 15)]\n","metadata":{"output":"rounds: Counter({'2': 376, '1': 334, '3': 258, '4': 140, '5': 123, '6': 62, '7': 30, '8': 14})\nseasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\nstages: [('group stage', 960), ('round of 16', 160), ('quarterfinals', 80), ('semifinals', 40), ('final', 15)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('rounds:', Counter(r['round'] for r in rows))\nprint('seasons:', sorted({r['season'] for r in rows}))\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nprint('stages:', Counter(r['stage'] for r in rows).most_common(20))\n\"","time":{"start":1788228515371,"end":1788228515374}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The FIFA dataset (18k players, FIFA 19/20 era) does NOT contain Flamengo, Palmeiras, Corinthians, or São Paulo clubs. It has Grêmio, Atlético Mineiro, Cruzeiro, Fluminense, Santos, Internacional, Botafogo, Bahia, etc. (20 players each — likely only the 2019 Libertadores participants or similar subset of Brazilian clubs).\n\nSo \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" simply can't be answered from this FIFA file. That's a dataset limitation, not a code bug. But the task says \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\" is an example question... The FIFA data is what it is. However, `get_club_overview('Flamengo')` returning 0 players is expected then. But wait — the club overview fuzzy match should at least say \"no FIFA squad found\". It returns player_count 0 — fine.\n\nBut `search_players(nationality='Brazil', club='Flamengo')` returning 0 is correct given the data. Fine.\n\nHowever, I should make sure search_players with club='Santos' works. Let me check the club matching. `text_key('Santos')` = 'santos' matches club 'Santos' exactly ✓. 'Santos Laguna' also contains... exact wins and comes first, good.\n\nNow, one more improvement: `get_club_overview` for clubs with FIFA squads works ('Santos', 'Grêmio', 'Botafogo', 'Fluminense', 'Cruzeiro', 'Atlético Mineiro', 'Internacional', 'Bahia', 'Vitória', 'Sport Recife'?, 'Chapecoense', 'Ceará', 'Paraná', 'Atlético Paranaense'?, 'América FC (Minas Gerais)'?). Let me test one.\n\nAlso \"Sport Club do Recife\" vs match-data name \"Sport Recife\": identity_key both → \"sport\"? Wait: identity_key(\"sport recife\") = \"sport recife\" (recife isn't generic). identity_key(\"sport club do recife\") → tokens [sport, club, do, recife]... \"sport club\" is in _GENERIC_PAIRS → removes \"sport club\"? tokens[-2:] == \"sport club\"? tokens = [sport, club, do, recife]; \" \".join(tokens[-2:]) = \"do recife\" no; then last token \"recife\" not generic. So identity = \"sport club do recife\" ≠ \"sport recife\". Mismatch! Hmm. The _GENERIC_PAIRS logic strips the pair when it's the LAST two tokens. \"sport club do recife\" has \"do\" — Portuguese \"of the\". A generic \"do\"/\"da\"/\"de\" handling would help: identity_key should probably also drop connector tokens (do, da, de, dos, das) when followed... but simple approach: drop connectors entirely from identity keys? \"club de regatas vasco da gama\" → \"club regatas vasco gama\" vs \"vasco da gama\" → \"vasco gama\". Not equal either.\n\nBut this matters only for team matching in match data (all sources use short names), and FIFA club names are a separate namespace (FIFA clubs like \"Clube Sport Marítimo\" are Portuguese clubs, not Brazilian). For get_club_overview, exact/prefix/contains matching on text_key: \"sport recife\" vs \"sport club do recife\" — contains fails. I could add a few alias mappings for FIFA club names in the club-matching: e.g. normalize club names through an alias map. Let me add a small `_CLUB_ALIASES` for FIFA club names → canonical match-data names: \n- \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → América Mineiro\n- \"Atlético Paranaense\" → Athletico Paranaense (alias \"atletico paranaense\" already maps ✓ via text_key? text_key(\"Atlético Paranaense\") = \"atletico paranaense\" which IS in _TEAM_ALIASES ✓)\n- \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → text_key = \"ceara sporting club\" in aliases ✓\n- \"Sport Club do Recife\" → \"sport club do recife\" — add alias → Sport Recife\n- \"Atlético Mineiro\" ✓ already\n- \"Clube Atlético Paranaense\"... exists? Only listed ones.\n\nActually simpler: in `get_club_overview` and `_match_club`, pass club names through a dedicated function `match_club_key` that tries _TEAM_ALIASES first (since _TEAM_ALIASES contains \"sport club do recife\" → \"Sport Recife\" ✓ and \"ceara sporting club\" ✓ and \"america fc minas gerais\" — but FIFA's is \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → text_key = \"america fc minas gerais\" ≠ \"america fc minas gerais\"! Wait _TEAM_ALIASES has \"america fc minas gerais\": \"América Mineiro\" ✓ (line 60). text_key(\"América FC (Minas Gerais)\") = \"america fc minas gerais\" — yes! matches ✓.\n\nSo the cleanest fix: a helper `club_identity(name)` that returns text_key(name) mapped through _TEAM_ALIASES if present. Then in get_club_overview use it for both sides. And in search_players club matching, apply the same: try alias first.\n\nBut careful: _TEAM_ALIASES contains generic-ish keys like \"santos\" → \"Santos\"? Not present (\"santos\" not in aliases). \"botafogo\" → \"Botafogo\"? \"botafogo rj\" is there but plain \"botafogo\" isn't — fine, text_key passes through.\n\nHmm wait, is it in scope? R8: \"filter players by nationality or club\" — \"Flamengo\" returns 0 (data limitation, acceptable), but \"Santos\" must work. Current exact match works for Santos. The alias integration is a bonus for overview correctness. I'll implement it modestly.\n\nPriority-wise, the REAL issues to fix:\n1. ✅ `_SOURCES` bug (fixed)\n2. Dedup across overlapping sources (standings correctness) — fix with windowed ordered-pair dedup\n3. Derby search bug (frozenset of raw names vs team_keys) + DERBIES ordering bug for (\"Flamengo\",\"Botafogo\")\n4. Round/stage filter \"final\" matching every knockout round — improve with exact round match preference. Actually let me check cup round labels first.\n5. Tests (R12) — big missing piece\n6. Check mcp tools JSON-serializable: `Match.to_dict` — all JSON-safe (dates are ISO strings, season int, etc.) ✓. `list_competitions` seasons list ✓. `Dataset.competitions()` — fine.\n\nAlso verify: `search_matches` with date_from/date_to in DD/MM/YYYY works (parse_date handles it) ✓.\n\nLet me also check the cup rounds and Libertadores stages for the finals query.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ab9b5f50017fMa2viCFAofVv","sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","messageID":"msg_05ab8d251001winvq8tdBcmn97"}}
