{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228884881,"sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_9847d68d71a346449879c297","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\nq = QueryEngine(Dataset())\nfor season, expected in [(2020,'Flamengo'), (2003,'Cruzeiro'), (2005,'Corinthians'), (2008,'São Paulo')]:\n    r = q.get_standings('brasileirao', season)\n    top = r['standings'][0] if r.get('standings') else None\n    print(season, '->', top['team'], top['points'], top['played'], 'games | complete:', r['table_complete'], '| expected champion:', expected)\n\""},"output":"2020 -> Flamengo 71 38 games | complete: True | expected champion: Flamengo\n2003 -> Cruzeiro 100 46 games | complete: True | expected champion: Cruzeiro\n2005 -> Corinthians 81 42 games | complete: True | expected champion: Corinthians\n2008 -> São Paulo 75 38 games | complete: True | expected champion: São Paulo\n","metadata":{"output":"2020 -> Flamengo 71 38 games | complete: True | expected champion: Flamengo\n2003 -> Cruzeiro 100 46 games | complete: True | expected champion: Cruzeiro\n2005 -> Corinthians 81 42 games | complete: True | expected champion: Corinthians\n2008 -> São Paulo 75 38 games | complete: True | expected champion: São Paulo\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\nq = QueryEngine(Dataset())\nfor season, expected in [(2020,'Flamengo'), (2003,'Cruzeiro'), (2005,'Corinthians'), (2008,'São Paulo')]:\n    r = q.get_standings('brasileirao', season)\n    top = r['standings'][0] if r.get('standings') else None\n    print(season, '->', top['team'], top['points'], top['played'], 'games | complete:', r['table_complete'], '| expected champion:', expected)\n\"","time":{"start":1788228884864,"end":1788228884880}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting: 109 conflicting-score dropped matches. The dropped ones have different scores than the kept ones. Are these the same match recorded differently by the sources (data quality), or different matches? Same date, same teams, same competition — they're certainly the same fixture (one source has wrong data, or penalty shootouts recorded differently: e.g., Copa do Brasil knockout recorded as 0-0 (regulation) in one source and 1-0 (after penalties?) in another — e.g., \"Joinville 1-0 Ituano\" vs \"Joinville 0-0 Ituano\" same day = same fixture, likely one includes penalty outcome. These are duplicates of the same fixture; keeping one is correct.\n\nAlso the count: dropped = len(pre)-len(kept) = 18163-17049 = 1114; my script's \"approx\" math was wrong but irrelevant — kept is 17049, matching.\n\nPriority order: novo first (kept for 2014-2015 Brazilian league), then Brasileirao_Matches, Cup, Libertadores, BR-Football last. Since we only use scores (not corners etc.), keeping novo's record is fine. But is novo's data more accurate than BR-Football's? Unknowable; either way it's one record per fixture which is what matters for standings. Real-world sanity check: 2019 table matches reality exactly, which is reassuring.\n\nLet me now double check a couple of other seasons' standings against reality:\n- 2020 Brasileirão champion: Flamengo (68 pts)\n- 2003 champion: Cruzeiro\n- 2005 champion: Corinthians\n- Copa do Brasil 2019: Athletico-PR champion (knockout — standings not applicable)\n\nQuick check for 2020 and 2003.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05abf5419001YKs1VE7XpJ3Udj","sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","messageID":"msg_05abee3230015c3XbZsSqenheE"}}
