{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788228923782,"sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_ccc2a9a267c14337b3c434df","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nfrom mcp import ClientSession, StdioServerParameters\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client\n\nasync def main():\n    params = StdioServerParameters(command=\"./venv/bin/python\", args=[\"-m\", \"brazilian_soccer_mcp\"])\n    async with stdio_client(params) as (read, write):\n        async with ClientSession(read, write) as session:\n            await session.initialize()\n            tools = await session.list_tools()\n            print(\"stdio OK, tools:\", len(tools.tools))\n            res = await session.call_tool(\"get_standings\", {\"competition\": \"brasileirao\", \"season\": 2019})\n            text = res.content[0].text\n            print(\"2019 champion via MCP:\", \"Flamengo\" in text and '\"points\": 90' in text)\n\nasyncio.run(main())\nEOF","timeout":120000},"output":"stdio OK, tools: 14\n2019 champion via MCP: True\n","metadata":{"output":"stdio OK, tools: 14\n2019 champion via MCP: True\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"./venv/bin/python << 'EOF'\nimport asyncio\nfrom mcp import ClientSession, StdioServerParameters\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client\n\nasync def main():\n    params = StdioServerParameters(command=\"./venv/bin/python\", args=[\"-m\", \"brazilian_soccer_mcp\"])\n    async with stdio_client(params) as (read, write):\n        async with ClientSession(read, write) as session:\n            await session.initialize()\n            tools = await session.list_tools()\n            print(\"stdio OK, tools:\", len(tools.tools))\n            res = await session.call_tool(\"get_standings\", {\"competition\": \"brasileirao\", \"season\": 2019})\n            text = res.content[0].text\n            print(\"2019 champion via MCP:\", \"Flamengo\" in text and '\"points\": 90' in text)\n\nasyncio.run(main())\nEOF","time":{"start":1788228923740,"end":1788228923781}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All standings match historical reality (2020: Flamengo 71 pts ✓, 2003: Cruzeiro ✓, 2005: Corinthians 81 ✓, 2008: São Paulo ✓). \n\nNow let me test the MCP server again end-to-end, then write the test suite. Also I should check `__init__.py` exports and maybe export `server` pieces. Let me also make sure `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp` starts the stdio server without crashing (run briefly).\n\nAlso check the README for accuracy later.\n\nTest plan (tests/):\n- tests/conftest.py: fixtures with session-scoped Dataset + QueryEngine\n- tests/test_normalize.py: team normalization (state suffix, accents, aliases, suffix codes), date parsing (ISO, BR format, with time), parse_int, parse_season, parse_money, identity_key, derby_name\n- tests/test_data_loader.py: all 6 CSVs load; matches/players counts; canonicalization; dedup (no ordered-pair duplicates within window per season+comp); resolve_team; matches_for_team; competitions()\n- tests/test_match_queries.py: search by team either side; by opponent pair; competition filter; season filter; date range; round/stage (\"final\" exact-first); result structure; summary record\n- tests/test_team_queries.py: get_team_stats (record correctness vs manual computation on raw data; venue filter; competition+season); head_to_head; get_team_competitions\n- tests/test_player_queries.py: name search; nationality filter; club filter + ratings; position/category; min/max overall; sort order; error on bad category\n- tests/test_competition_queries.py: standings computed from matches (verify points formula, ordering, champion == re-derived), season summary, compare seasons\n- tests/test_stats_queries.py: avg goals per match matches manual calc; home/away win rates; biggest wins sorted; get_best_records; derbies search\n- tests/test_cross_file.py: get_club_overview combines match record + FIFA squad (Santos has squad; Flamengo matches>0)\n- tests/test_mcp_server.py: server has tools; list_tools returns >= 12 tools; call a couple of tools end-to-end; server entrypoint runs stdio (maybe just check create_server works).\n\nFor test MCP server: use asyncio; `await server.list_tools()` and `await server.call_tool(...)`. Verified earlier that works.\n\nAlso add BDD-style test names matching the TASK.md gherkin? The task says \"Use BDD scenarios\" as testing approach — pytest with descriptive names is fine; I'll include a bdd-style test file using pytest parametrization with given/when/then naming to honor the spec.\n\nLet me also double-check that `from brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, Match, Player, QueryEngine` exports don't break — Match/Player exported ✓.\n\nOne more thing: `python -m brazilian_soccer_mcp` — the `run(\"stdio\")` call. Let me verify signature `MCPServer.run(transport)`. Earlier dir showed `run`. Quick smoke: spawn with timeout and send initialize request? Simpler: run with a timeout and check it doesn't crash immediately; or use mcp client stdio. Let me do a real client test using the SDK's stdio client to prove the entrypoint works.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05abfe8ad001O2LpvnFn8lRAGR","sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","messageID":"msg_05abf5ae1001UMWpu09o5tARVg"}}
