{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788229000412,"sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_0ef5b1e0a5a742819dd63a3e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Shared fixtures: session-scoped dataset and query engine.\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef dataset() -> Dataset:\n    return Dataset()\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef engine(dataset: Dataset) -> QueryEngine:\n    return QueryEngine(dataset)\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-242ce4667ad2/tests/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-75154ofp/retort-242ce4667ad2/tests/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/conftest.py","time":{"start":1788229000404,"end":1788229000410}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Clear. Now I'll write the test suite. Let me create tests/ directory with conftest.py and several test modules. I'll write comprehensive tests covering R2-R12.\n\nconftest.py:\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import Dataset, QueryEngine\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef dataset():\n    return Dataset()\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef engine(dataset):\n    return QueryEngine(dataset)\n```\n\nDataset load takes ~1.2s — session scope is fine.\n\ntest files as planned. Let me be careful with assertions to match actual data:\n\n- Dataset loads: len(matches) > 15000, len(players) == 18207, all 5 match sources present, player source count == 18207.\n- resolve_team: \"Palmeiras-SP\" → \"Palmeiras\"; \"Sao Paulo\" → \"São Paulo\"; \"Palmeiras\" → \"Palmeiras\".\n- matches_for_team(\"Flamengo\") non-empty; every match contains Flamengo.\n- search_matches(team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\") → total>0; every match has both teams; summary has team_a_wins etc.\n- search team \"either\": team-only filter covers home and away roles: check both roles present.\n- season filter: season=2023 with team=Palmeiras → all season 2023.\n- date range: date_from=\"2023-01-01\", date_to=\"2023-12-31\" → all within 2023.\n- Brazilian date format: date_from=\"01/01/2023\".\n- competition filter: competition=\"Copa do Brasil\" → all competition == Copa do Brasil. Also \"brasileirao\" alias → \"Brasileirão\". \"libertadores\" → Libertadores.\n- stage: competition=\"libertadores\", round_or_stage=\"final\" → all stage exact \"final\" (test: stage label equals final).\n- get_team_stats(\"Corinthians\", season=2022): record played == 38? Wait — with dedup, Corinthians 2022 in Brasileirão should be 38 total (19 home, 19 away). But data anomalies might exist. Safer assertions: record fields present, played == wins+draws+losses, played > 0, home record played < all record played. And goals consistency. Cross-check vs manual computation: compute record directly from dataset matches for canonical team and compare with engine output.\n- head_to_head(\"Palmeiras\",\"Santos\"): record sums equal total matches with goals; both directions consistent: h2h(a,b).team_a_wins == h2h(b,a).team_b_wins.\n- search_players(name=\"Neymar\") finds Neymar Jr overall 92. Name search \"gabriel\" returns players containing token.\n- nationality filter: nationality=\"Brazil\" → all contain \"Brazil\" (text_key containment: 'brazil' in 'brazil' ✓ — but nationality \"Brazil\" might also be... fine). club filter \"Santos\" exact — all returned players' club == \"Santos\"? _match_club returns exact+prefix+contains: 'Santos Laguna' is prefix ('santos laguna'.startswith('santos') ✓) so returned set may include Santos Laguna players. Test: first N are exact club Santos? Sorted by overall across all. Safer: assert every player whose club=='Santos' among results? Hmm. Let me assert: all(\"santos\" in text_key(p[\"club\"]) for p in results) and any(p[\"club\"]==\"Santos\" for p in results). Also results have overall ratings.\n- position_category=\"forward\" → all positions in forward set. min_overall=85 → all overall>=85. Bad category → error key.\n- nationality+club combined: club=\"Ceará\" (alias from Ceará Sporting Club) → 20 players all Brazilian? Not necessarily all Brazilian nationality (probably yes for Ceará). Safer: total_players == 20 and all players' club text_key == \"ceara sporting club\".\n- get_standings(\"brasileirao\", 2019): champion Flamengo 90 pts; complete True; 20 teams; all teams 38 played; points == 3*wins+draws; sorted by points desc; positions 1..20; note fields. Also cross-check re-derivation: compute table from ds.matches and compare champion.\n- standings error case: get_standings(\"libertadores\", 1900) → error.\n- get_season_summary(2019): champions['Brasileirão']['team']=='Flamengo'; competitions include Brasileirão with avg goals.\n- compare_seasons(2018, 2019) has both.\n- get_competition_stats(\"serie a\"): matches == total with goals; avg goals = manual calc; home_win_rate between 0-100; biggest_wins length <= top; verify biggest win is max |diff| in the pool. Also cross-competition: competition=None stats cover everything.\n- get_best_records(venue=\"home\", season=2023, min_matches=5): rankings all win_rate >= others; each has min played; error for venue=\"middle\".\n- search_derbies(season=2023): all matches are derby pairs; total > 0; matches have derby names.\n- get_team_competitions(\"Palmeiras\"): includes Brasileirão; seasons sorted.\n- get_club_overview(\"Santos\"): fifa_squad player_count == 46 (Santos 20 + Santos Laguna 26 = 46!). Hmm — earlier output said 46 which includes Santos Laguna. matched_clubs includes both. Test: player_count >= 20; avg_overall is float; top_players non-empty sorted by overall desc; all_time_record played > 500.\n- get_club_overview(\"Flamengo\"): matches exist, fifa_squad player_count == 0 (no Flamengo in FIFA) — assert >= 0 and matches exist. Fine.\n- list_teams/list_competitions basic structure.\n- MCP server tests: asyncio: list_tools has 14 unique names; call_tool search_matches returns content with JSON containing \"total_matches\"; get_standings 2019 contains Flamengo. Also test create_server registers tools without duplicates.\n- BDD-style: a test class named per the gherkin scenarios from TASK.md:\n  - \"Scenario: Find matches between two teams\" — given data loaded; when search between Flamengo/Fluminense; then each match has date, scores, competition.\n  - \"Scenario: Get team statistics\" — when stats for Palmeiras season 2023; then wins/losses/draws/goals present.\n  I'll implement these as functions with those names in test_bdd_scenarios.py.\n- normalize tests: parse_date formats; parse_season; parse_int (\"2\", 2.7, \"NA\"); parse_money (\"€110.5M\" → 110500000.0, \"€565K\" → 565000); strip_team_suffix (\"Palmeiras-SP\"); identity_key (\"Fortaleza FC\" == \"Fortaleza\"); derby_name both orders; text_key.\n- data quality: dedup invariant — no two matches with same (competition, season, identity pair) within 3 days: recompute from ds.matches and assert.\n- Team name variation requirement: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Palmeiras\", \"São Paulo FC\"? resolve_team equality test.\n- Performance: simple lookup < 2s: measure search_matches(team=...) elapsed < 2.0; aggregate < 5s: get_competition_stats < 5.0. (Loose but per spec.)\n\nAlso test __main__/server entrypoint already covered by stdio client test — but that spawns subprocess (slow ~2-3s, fine). I'll include it but mark it clearly. Hmm, spawning stdio client inside pytest should work. It took a couple of seconds earlier. Keep it.\n\nTotal tests maybe ~70. Good.\n\nOne caution: tests must not depend on network. All local.\n\nAlso: should I keep the `Match.date` as str? fine.\n\nAlso check `Dataset()` default data dir — when tests run from repo root, DEFAULT_DATA_DIR is relative to module file → repo/data/kaggle ✓ regardless of cwd.\n\nLet me also add pyproject/pytest config? Not needed; pytest discovers tests/ automatically. But pytest-cov is installed; the grader may run coverage. Fine.\n\nAlso update README with usage instructions (nice-to-have; quick).\n\nLet me write the tests now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ac11ccd001XAn7pO7nczhHmb","sessionID":"ses_fa54e4cfeffeF35792XylHPXI3","messageID":"msg_05ac01bad001vcUWX90p04tDDj"}}
